******************************************************************************
                                   Overview
******************************************************************************
This is a GUI library specificaly designed for  VGA 640X480X16 mode.  It uses
very fast assembler routines for the graphical functions.  
This library gives the capability of programming in graphics mode while using
text mode type functions.  It supports a series of text mode functions which
enables the library to simulate a text mode screen of  80 columns by 30 rows.
If text is written to a specific loction of the screen, it may be read later,
the same way as a text mode program would allow it to be read.  Besides text 
mode routines it also supports graphics functions.

Using this library anyone with a basic knowledge of programming in text mode 
can write a program in Graphics mode.

The example program provided has all the functionalities provided with this 
library including its hyper text help facility.

To make your first program, just use the example as a basic shell and add on
to it.

Librarys provided are compiled with MSC 5.1  BorlandC 3.1  PowerC 2.2

The source code for the library is very portable.  Most compilers will
compile the source code without any changes.  Source code for this 
library is available. For details refer to the end of the document or
the DEMO.EXE program.

